# Raw GPS traces from Strava. These hold your exact position, with a
# timestamp roughly every second, so they stay on your computer and are
# never published. The cards drawn from them carry no coordinates and are
# safe to publish.
*.gpx

# Python's cache of compiled files. Rebuilt automatically, never worth
# keeping.
__pycache__/

# Editor and tool settings belonging to this machine only.
.claude/

# The full size card PNGs. These are yours to print and share, and stay on
# your computer. The site only needs the .webp copies beside them, which
# are a seventh of the weight. Noise does not compress, so committing the
# PNGs added about 54 MB to the repository's history on every run.
cards/*.png

# OpenStreetMap extracts, one per walk. The site never loads them: they
# are only what make_postcards.py draws the ground from. They also give
# the exact streets a walk went down, which is finer than the city the
# cards are willing to name, so they stay on this computer. get_maps.py
# fetches them again if they are ever lost.
walks/*.geojson

# The earlier plates prototype, which postcards.html replaced. Kept on
# disk and in the history, but not published: plates/ only ever held two
# of the twelve walks, so walks.html would go out half finished.
walks.html
walk-plates-spec.md
make_plates.py
plates/
